The '''Castejón Metro Iznájar Line''' ({{Lang-bl|Linia de Metro de Castejón a Iznájar}}) is a [[W:Rapid transit|subway]] line in [[Castejón]], Balisca, operated by [[Castejón Metro]]. The line runs between [[Amanecer Station]] in [[Calañas]] and [[Caatiba Station]] in [[Trinacria]]. The official name is '''Line 6 Iznájar Line'''.

The line's name originates from the [[Arabic language|Arabic]] phrase ''Hisn Ashar'', meaning "stone castle" or "fortress of ten", referring to the masonry [[W:Coastal defence and fortification|coastal fortification]] that it passes over in [[Mercadero]] as part of the western approach of the [[Salto Bay Bridge]]. On maps, diagrams and signboards, the line is shown using the color [[W:Shades of blue|strong blue]], and its stations are given numbers using the letter "I". 

